{"step_index":280,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-05T18:35:47Z","input_tokens":4539,"cache_read_tokens":32880,"output_tokens":2374,"thinking":"**Analyzing Configuration Timing**\n\nI've discovered a very brief wait time configured: \"timing\\_ball\\_wait\" is only 0.5 seconds. I see the program logs a debug message indicating a wait for the ball animation, based on this config, in the `_check_capture_result` method. This seems quite short for any meaningful wait.\n\n\n**Revising Active Polling Logic**\n\nI've realized the active polling is the most recent change. The user's complaint about slow 'X' presses likely predates its implementation, as I suspected. The \"esteticos\" comment supports this. My focus shifts to the aesthetic improvements mentioned and verifying the Active Polling's impact.\n\n\n**Clarifying Post-Implementation Status**\n\nI'm now focusing on the user's latest updates. The user reported, \"el ditto aparece sobre el ocr de mensaje de confirm\" - this appears to be a clue. I'm reviewing their statement in the broader context of the \"Ditto plan\" and the confirmation messages. It seems the issue isn't timing but that the Ditto is appearing during OCR.\n\n\n**Pinpointing X-Press Timing**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the X-press speed during ball capture. The user has explicitly stated the bot's X press is too slow, and there's no configurable parameter. The code shows the sequence `left, X, right, X` with short durations of 0.02 seconds. I need to understand if the delay is a configuration parameter, or simply the hardcoded press duration in `base.py` and the `time.sleep` call. The focus is on implementing configurable timing.\n\n\n**Implementing Spam Delay Control**\n\nI've crafted a plan, focusing on adding a new config parameter, `timing_capture_spam_delay`, to control the 'X' press delay during ball capture, as requested. The plan includes default values and updates to `base.py` and `config.json`. I'm also mindful of the recent aesthetic adjustments the user made, which will need to be accounted for. The next step is implementing the planned delay parameter and verifying the changes.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":true,\"Summary\":\"Plan de implementación para parametrizar el delay del spam de la X durante la captura.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"## Plan de Mejora: Control del Spam de Captura (Ditto)\\n\\n### [Goal Description] (目的 - Mokuteki)\\nEl problema principal que descubriste es que el *delay* al presionar 'X' cuando el Ditto es atrapado era confuso y no había un parámetro claro para controlarlo en la configuración. \\nEl objetivo de este plan es **parametrizar el delay del spam de teclas** para que el usuario (*bebito*) tenga control total sobre qué tan rápido se limpia la UI superpuesta, garantizando que el OCR lea instantáneamente.\\n\\n### Proposed Changes\\n\\n#### [MODIFY] `config.json`\\nAñadir un parámetro explícito para controlar la velocidad del bucle (el *spam*).\\n```json\\n  \\\"timing_ball_wait\\\": 0.5,\\n  \\\"timing_capture_settle\\\": 2.5,\\n  \\\"timing_capture_spam_delay\\\": 0.1,  // <-- [NUEVO] Controla el delay del spam de X\\n```\\n\\n#### [MODIFY] `src/modes/base.py`\\nEnlazar el nuevo parámetro al bucle de captura para que ya no esté \\\"*hardcodeado*\\\".\\n```python\\n    def _check_capture_result(self):\\n        ball_wait   = float(self.config.get(\\\"timing_ball_wait\\\", 0.5))\\n        settle_time = float(self.config.get(\\\"timing_capture_settle\\\", 2.5))\\n        spam_delay  = float(self.config.get(\\\"timing_capture_spam_delay\\\", 0.1)) # <-- [NUEVO]\\n\\n        self.log(f\\\"⏳ Waiting {ball_wait}s for ball animation...\\\", \\\"DEBUG\\\")\\n        time.sleep(ball_wait)\\n\\n        for _ in range(60):\\n            if not self.bot.running:\\n                return False\\n                \\n            # ACTIVE POLLING: Destruimos ventanas